0.16087912087912087,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.139497055195257,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.04478941016751581,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":2.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.01887329241492473,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":68.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.42194093206139927,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.2212843090097616,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":1.0000001e-05,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Icahn Enterprises L.P., through its subsidiaries engages in the investment, energy, automotive, food packaging, real estate, home fashion and pharma in the United States and internationally. The Investment segment invests its proprietary capital through various private investment funds; and it provides investment advisory, administrative, and back-office services to the investment funds. The Energy segment engages in refining and marketing petroleum in the form of gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, and distillates; renewable fuels business refines renewable feedstocks, such as soybean oil, corn oil, and other related renewable feedstocks into renewable diesel and markets renewable products; and nitrogen fertilizer business produces and markets nitrogen fertilizers in the form of urea ammonium nitrate and ammonia. The Automotive segment engages in repair and maintenance of automotive; sale of installed parts or materials related to automotive services; and sale of automotive aftermarket parts and retailed merchandise. The Food Packaging segment produces and sells cellulosic, fibrous, and plastic casings used to prepare and pack processed meat products. The Real Estate segment consists of investment properties, including land, retail, office, and industrial properties; and development and sale of single-family homes; and the operations of a resort and two country clubs. The Home Fashion segment manufactures, sources, markets, distributes, and sells home fashion consumer products. The Pharma segment offers pharmaceutical products and services; and develops approved therapies and product candidates. Icahn Enterprises L.P. was incorporated in 1987 and is headquartered in Sunny Isles Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ted  Papapostolou | President, CEO, Secretary & Director of Icahn Enterprises GP Inc | Age 44 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $712K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Icahn Enterprises L.P. - Deposi is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.6B market cap on $9.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -12% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $654M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 42.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 5714% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 3218% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":32.183825638084315},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 88% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Should Third Quarter Loss Require Action From Icahn Enterprises (IEP) Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-iep/icahn-enterprises/news/should-third-quarter-loss-require-action-from-icahn-enterpri","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794554139.909,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Icahn Enterprises (IEP) Undervalued As Sales Rose But Losses Returned?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-iep/icahn-enterprises/news/is-icahn-enterprises-iep-undervalued-as-sales-rose-but-losse","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794464614.553,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing Icahn Enterprises (NASDAQ:IEP) & Diamondback Energy (NASDAQ:FANG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/reviewing-icahn-enterprises-nasdaqiep-diamondback-energy-nasdaqfang.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794194925.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (IEP) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_IEP_Price_Events_110626101802_1793978282.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793978282.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Analysis: Icahn Enterprises (NASDAQ:IEP) versus Dynagas LNG Partners (NYSE:DLNG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/financial-analysis-icahn-enterprises-nasdaqiep-versus-dynagas-lng-partners-nysedlng.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793957342.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.885,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title"